			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Simplify binary name and Tauri identifier to production values\n\nReplace the verbose development profile identifier `DevelopmentNodeEnvironment_MicrosoftVSCodeDependency_24NodeVersion_Bundle_Clean_Debug_ElectronProfile_EsbuildCompiler_Mountain` with the canonical `Mountain` name across Cargo.toml (binary, library, default-run, package name) and tauri.conf.json (productName, identifier).\n\nUpdate the Tauri identifier from `land.editor.binary.development.node.environment.microsoft.vscode.dependency.node.24.bundle.clean.debug.electron.profile.esbuild.compiler.mountain` to `fiddee.editor.binary` to align with the FIDDEE product branding. Reorganize resource mappings in tauri.conf.json for logical grouping, inline externalBin and targets arrays, and remove deprecated backup files.\n\nImpact: Clean production-ready naming for the Mountain native backend binary and Tauri application identity.",
			"SHA": "77a75c9bdb707be4804713af9e62c573bc3a5505"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-11T02:40:13Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1770,
				4
			],
			"Message": "build(Mountain): Configure development build profile with Node 24 VS Code dependency\n\nRename the Mountain binary and library to a descriptive development profile identifier: DevelopmentNodeEnvironment_MicrosoftVSCodeDependency_24NodeVersion_Bundle_Clean_Debug_ElectronProfile_EsbuildCompiler_Mountain. Update Tauri configuration to match with new productName and identifier using the land.editor.binary domain.\n\nAdd comprehensive resource mappings for Sky editor UI targets (Browser, BrowserProxy, Bundled, Electron, Favicon, Isolation, Manifest.json, Mountain, Static assets, Worker.js, extensions manifest, index.html, product.json, robots.txt, _astro) and Cocoon bootstrap implementation. Reorganize resource list for clarity and remove shell integration scripts from bundle.\n\nThis configuration enables a clean debug build targeting Electron profile with esbuild compiler against VS Code dependencies at Node 24.",
			"SHA": "2e0657c485e7225c5e5638967d9c4aa04d7bdc40"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-11T02:29:54Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1768,
				15
			],
			"Message": "style(Mountain): Normalize formatting across IPC handlers and Cocoon management\n\nApply consistent formatting to Vine gRPC notification calls across WindServiceHandlers dispatchers (Configuration, Sky, Storage, TreeView), ExtensionHost debug services, NativeHost openExternal, and the main mountain_ipc_invoke router. Condense multi-line variable bindings in CocoonManagement restart loop and terminal property updates. Fix shell integration redirect syntax (2>/dev/null → 2> /dev/null). Add whitespace separation between Send/Sync impl blocks in MountainEnvironment.\n\nNo functional changes — purely cosmetic improvements for readability and consistency.",
			"SHA": "4766ea68e2da6a8cfb55150513fdd00918d1d080"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-11T02:22:30Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1768,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Seed Cocoon with existing terminals and expand IPC method handlers\n\nCocoon's gRPC channel opens after the workbench restores terminals, leaving `vscode.window.terminals` empty for extensions that read it synchronously in `activate()`. After the sidecar connects, iterate `ApplicationState.Feature.Terminals` and resend each open terminal via the `$acceptTerminalOpened` notification so the terminal list is populated before extensions activate.\n\nAlso extend the Effect request routing matchers:\n- FileWatcher: add `Register` and `Unregister` methods\n- Storage: add `GetItems` method\n- Task: add `terminate_task` and `Task.Terminate` methods\n- Workspace: add `RequestResourceTrust`, `IsResourceTrusted`, `Save`, `SaveAs`, `saveAll`, `SaveAll` methods\n\nFix minor shell integration syntax: `2> /dev/null` → `2>/dev/null`.\n\nImpact: Extensions no longer see an empty terminal list on startup, and the Mountain backend now handles the full surface of FileWatcher, Storage, Task, and Workspace IPC requests from Cocoon.",
			"SHA": "ec51929472623ef48d7a09a541edc668f24c0f6b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-10T20:22:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1768,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Move Cocoon restart loop to dedicated thread with LocalSet\n\nThe Cocoon sidecar restart logic was running via `tokio::task::spawn_local` on Tauri's single-threaded runtime, but `LaunchAndManageCocoonSideCar` is `!Send` because it holds `parking_lot` guards across `.await` points. This created a soundness risk on the shared executor.\n\nReplace with a dedicated OS thread (`cocoon-restart`) that owns a `current_thread` Tokio runtime wrapped in a `LocalSet`. The restart receiver, `AppHandle`, and `Arc<MountainEnvironment>` are all `Send` and cross the thread boundary safely. The `LocalSet` enables `spawn_local` for the async restart loop without requiring the future to be `Send`.\n\nImpact: Eliminates the `!Send` future on the main Tauri runtime, maintains exponential backoff restart semantics, and isolates Cocoon lifecycle management on its own executor.",
			"SHA": "38160a1a67b1803a20b230914efc91e76bb31a2c"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1781446803999
}